# Every text file checks out with LF on every OS.
#
# Measured 2026-09-16: on a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, git rewrote committed eval
# records with CRLF, so the SHA-256 each record stores over its prereg no longer matched the file
# (a413a3fa... over LF vs 85fb01fe... over CRLF) and the eval-history check failed. CI runs on
# Linux, where this never happens, so it could only ever fail on a Windows machine. Anything this
# repo hashes as bytes -- eval records, panel locks, seat answers -- must not depend on the OS
# that checked it out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
